id: pm-gh1731
title: "GH-1731: ship a bounded, version-matched migration record in the npm package now that CHANGELOG.md is excluded"
description: "Since pm-jndg9a dropped the generated CHANGELOG.md from the tarball, an installed pm has no local copy of its Migrate: notes. Extension authors adapting to a contract change have to fetch the upstream changelog, guess from failing tests or read dist sources. On 2026-11-14 two agents adapting 12 fleet extensions from 2026.11.7 to 2026.11.14 both fetched and grepped the upstream file. The Migrate: text comes from the contract_change field that pm-changelog renders (pm-gh1657 owns the migration line itself). Generating the bounded record belongs in the pm-changelog repo; this repo ships it and keeps it inside the tarball budget. Option B, a pm migrations --from <version> read over the same data, can come after the shipped file exists."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,changelog,"gh:1731",packaging,release
created_at: "2026-11-14T15:41:55.575Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T15:46:06.583Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The published tarball contains a generated migration record (for example docs/MIGRATIONS.md) holding only entries with a Migrate: note, newest first, bounded by release count or size; The record is produced by pm-changelog from contract_change data, not hand-written, and a check fails when it drifts from the tracker; The tarball size gate covers the new file and stays within budget; npx and bunx installs of the release can read the record offline"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: medium
expected_result: "An installed pm package carries a bounded Migrate: record for recent releases that is readable offline"
actual_result: "The installed package has no Migrate: text, so adapting an extension needs the upstream changelog"
